      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i need help writing a rejection email for a candidate. they made it to the final round for a senior backend engineer role here in austin but we decided to go with someone else. it's a tough one because they were actually really strong technically and had great culture fit, so i don't want to burn the bridge or sound like a robot. can you help me draft something professional but kind?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Writing a rejection email can be a delicate matter, especially when the candidate was a strong contender. You want to convey your gratitude for their interest in the role while also being clear about your decision. I'd be happy to help you draft a rejection email that's both professional and kind.\n\nHere's a sample email that you can use as a starting point:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the status of your application for the Senior Backend Engineer role at [Company Name]. We were truly impressed by your technical skills and your passion for the industry, and we appreciate the time you took to interview with us.\n\nAfter careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and experience align more closely with the specific needs of our team at this time. Please know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were genuinely excited about the potential you brought to the table.\n\nI want to emphasize that this decision is in no way a reflection on your abilities or potential as a candidate. You have a strong technical foundation and a great fit for our company culture, and we have no doubt that you will find a role that is a great match for you.\n\nThank you again for your interest in [Company Name",
